Article 3 A circuit court shall adjudicate or handle the following cases within the circuit area that shall be accepted by the Supreme People's Court:
(1) major and complex first-instance administrative cases nationwide;
(2) first-instance civil and commercial cases with significant national influence;
(3) cases appealed against first-instance administrative or civil and commercial judgments or rulings made by a Higher People's Court;
(4) cases applying for retrial against legally effective administrative or civil and commercial judgments, rulings, or mediation documents made by a Higher People's Court;
(5) criminal petition cases;
(6) cases in which a retrial is initiated in accordance with statutory powers;
(7) cases applying for reconsideration against decisions on fines or detention made by a Higher People's Court;
(8) cases in which a Higher People's Court reports to the Supreme People's Court for a ruling or decision on jurisdictional issues;
(9) cases in which a Higher People's Court requests approval for extending the adjudication time limit;
(10) civil and commercial cases involving Hong Kong, Macao, and Taiwan, and judicial assistance cases;
(11) other cases that the Supreme People's Court considers shall be adjudicated or handled by a circuit court.
A circuit court shall, according to law, handle matters of letters and visits submitted to the Supreme People's Court within the circuit area.
